        "children": [
         {
          "id": "v2-proposal-j3-074410-j3-gp-a",
          "type": "part",
          "label": "a",
          "prompt": "A rectangular field of area $150\\text{ m}^2$ is fenced all round and divided into two equal paddocks by a fence parallel to one pair of its sides, as shown.\n\nFind the dimensions of the field that minimise the length of fencing, and the minimum length.",
          "answerSpaceMm": 80,
          "questionDiagrams": [
           {
            "id": "v2-proposal-j3-074410-j3-gp-a-diagram",
            "format": "tikz",
            "widthMm": 55,
            "code": "% mathsmap-diagram-colours {\"version\":1,\"kind\":\"geometry\",\"base\":[],\"semantic\":[],\"reference\":\"j3 guided practice a\"}\n\\begin{tikzpicture}[x=1cm,y=1cm,line width=0.8pt,every node/.style={font=\\fontsize{10}{12}\\selectfont,text=black}]\n\\special{dvisvgm:raw <metadata data-graph-strokes=\"1\"/>}\n\\draw[black] (0,0) rectangle (4.4,2.2);\n\\draw[black] (2.2,0)--(2.2,2.2);\n\\path (0,0)--(0,2.2) node[midway,left] {$x$};\n\\path (0,0)--(4.4,0) node[midway,below] {$y$};\n\\end{tikzpicture}"
           }
          ],
          "answer": {
           "short": "$x=10\\text{ m}$ and $y=15\\text{ m}$. The minimum length of fencing is $60\\text{ m}$.",
           "worked": "The fence has three lengths of $x$ and two of $y$.\n$$\\begin{align*}xy&=150\\\\y&=\\frac{150}{x}\\\\L&=3x+2y\\\\L(x)&=3x+\\frac{300}{x},\\qquad x>0.\\end{align*}$$\n$$\\begin{align*}L'(x)&=3-\\frac{300}{x^2}=0\\\\x^2&=100\\\\x&=10\\quad(x>0)\\\\L''(x)&=\\frac{600}{x^3}>0\\quad\\text{for all }x>0.\\end{align*}$$\nSo $x=10$ gives the global minimum.\n$$\\begin{align*}y&=\\frac{150}{10}=15\\\\L(10)&=3(10)+\\frac{300}{10}=60\\text{ m}.\\end{align*}$$"
          }
         },
         {
          "id": "v2-proposal-j3-074410-j3-gp-b",
          "type": "part",
          "label": "b",
          "prompt": "An open box with a square base is to have a volume of $32\\text{ cm}^3$.\n\nFind the base side length that minimises the surface area of the box, and the minimum surface area.",
          "answerSpaceMm": 80,
          "answer": {
           "short": "Base side length $4\\text{ cm}$. The minimum surface area is $48\\text{ cm}^2$.",
           "worked": "Let the base side be $x$ cm and the height $h$ cm.\n$$\\begin{align*}x^2h&=32\\\\h&=\\frac{32}{x^2}\\\\S&=x^2+4xh\\\\S(x)&=x^2+\\frac{128}{x},\\qquad x>0.\\end{align*}$$\n$$\\begin{align*}S'(x)&=2x-\\frac{128}{x^2}=0\\\\2x^3&=128\\\\x^3&=64\\\\x&=4\\\\S''(x)&=2+\\frac{256}{x^3}>0\\quad\\text{for all }x>0.\\end{align*}$$\nSo $x=4$ gives the global minimum.\n$$S(4)=16+\\frac{128}{4}=48\\text{ cm}^2.$$"
          }
         }
        ]
       },
