          "label": "a",
          "prompt": "A bushwalker is 3 km from the nearest point $A$ on a straight road. She wants to reach, as soon as possible, a point $B$ on the road a further 10 km from $A$.\n\nShe walks through scrub at 4 km/h to a point on the road $x$ km from $A$, then walks along the road to $B$ at 5 km/h.\n\nFind the value of $x$ that minimises the time taken, and the minimum time.",
          "answerSpaceMm": 90,
          "questionDiagrams": [
           {
            "id": "v2-proposal-j4-074410-j4-gp-a-diagram",
