           }
          ],
          "answer": {
           "short": "$x=4$. The minimum time is $\\dfrac{49}{20}=2.45$ hours.",
           "worked": "$$T(x)=\\frac{\\sqrt{9+x^2}}{4}+\\frac{10-x}{5},\\qquad0\\le x\\le10.$$\n$$\\begin{align*}T'(x)&=\\frac{x}{4\\sqrt{9+x^2}}-\\frac15=0\\\\5x&=4\\sqrt{9+x^2}\\\\25x^2&=16(9+x^2)\\\\9x^2&=144\\\\x^2&=16\\\\x&=4\\quad(0\\le x\\le10).\\end{align*}$$\nCheck: $5(4)=20=4\\sqrt{25}$.\n$$T''(x)=\\frac{9}{4(9+x^2)^{3/2}}>0\\quad\\text{for all }x.$$\nSo $x=4$ gives the global minimum.\n$$T(4)=\\frac54+\\frac65=\\frac{49}{20}\\text{ hours}.$$"
          }
         },
