          "id": "v2-proposal-j4-074410-j4-gp-b",
          "type": "part",
          "label": "b",
          "prompt": "A swimmer in difficulty is 40 m from a straight beach, directly out from a point $P$. A lifesaver on the beach is 120 m from $P$.\n\nShe runs along the beach at 5 m/s to a point $x$ m from her starting position, then swims straight to the swimmer at 3 m/s.\n\nFind the value of $x$ that minimises the time taken, and the minimum time.",
          "answerSpaceMm": 100,
          "questionDiagrams": [
           {
            "id": "v2-proposal-j4-074410-j4-gp-b-diagram",
