            "code": "% mathsmap-diagram-colours {\"version\":1,\"kind\":\"geometry\",\"base\":[],\"semantic\":[],\"reference\":\"j4 guided practice b\"}\n\\begin{tikzpicture}[x=1cm,y=1cm,line width=0.8pt,every node/.style={font=\\fontsize{10}{12}\\selectfont,text=black},>=stealth]\n\\special{dvisvgm:raw <metadata data-graph-strokes=\"1\"/>}\n\\coordinate (L) at (0,1.8);\n\\coordinate (P) at (4.8,1.8);\n\\coordinate (S) at (4.8,0);\n\\coordinate (Q) at (3.2,1.8);\n\\draw[black] (L)--(P);\n\\draw[black] (P)--(S);\n\\draw[black] (Q)--(S);\n\\draw[black,line width=0.4pt] (4.56,1.8)--(4.56,1.56)--(4.8,1.56);\n\\fill[black] (L) circle (1.6pt);\n\\fill[black] (Q) circle (1.6pt);\n\\fill[black] (S) circle (1.6pt);\n\\node[above right] at (P) {$P$};\n\\node[below] at (L) {lifesaver};\n\\node[below] at (S) {swimmer};\n\\path (L)--(Q) node[midway,above] {$x\\text{ m}$};\n\\path (P)--(S) node[midway,right] {$40\\text{ m}$};\n\\draw[black,<->,line width=0.5pt] (0,2.9)--(4.8,2.9) node[midway,fill=white,inner sep=2pt] {$120\\text{ m}$};\n\\end{tikzpicture}"
           }
          ],
          "answer": {
           "short": "$x=90$. The minimum time is $\\dfrac{104}{3}\\approx34.7$ seconds.",
           "worked": "She runs $x$ m, then swims $\\sqrt{40^2+(120-x)^2}$ m.\n$$T(x)=\\frac{x}{5}+\\frac{\\sqrt{1600+(120-x)^2}}{3},\\qquad0\\le x\\le120.$$\n$$\\begin{align*}T'(x)&=\\frac15-\\frac{120-x}{3\\sqrt{1600+(120-x)^2}}=0\\\\5(120-x)&=3\\sqrt{1600+(120-x)^2}\\\\25(120-x)^2&=9\\left(1600+(120-x)^2\\right)\\\\16(120-x)^2&=14400\\\\(120-x)^2&=900\\\\120-x&=\\pm30\\\\x&=90\\text{ or }150.\\end{align*}$$\nOnly $x=90$ is in the domain. Check: $5(30)=150=3\\sqrt{2500}$.\n$$T''(x)=\\frac{1600}{3\\left(1600+(120-x)^2\\right)^{3/2}}>0\\quad\\text{for all }x.$$\nSo $x=90$ gives the global minimum.\n$$T(90)=\\frac{90}{5}+\\frac{\\sqrt{2500}}{3}=18+\\frac{50}{3}=\\frac{104}{3}\\text{ s}.$$"
